ECOMMERCE:

    Base Product class extended into Electronics and Clothing.
    Showed how inheritance organizes product categories.
    Used DiscountMixin to apply offers flexibly.
    Added ExportMixin to export product info.
    Demonstrated clean separation of business logic and utility features.
    Modeled a real-world e-commerce system.
    Improved reusability of discount and export features across product types.


FOOD TRACKING:

    Base Order extended into PizzaOrder and BurgerOrder.
    Showed inheritance for handling different food items.
    Used TrackMixin for real-time order tracking.
    Added InvoiceMixin for billing functionality.
    dded RewardMixin for customer loyalty points.
    Simulated a food delivery application.
    Learned to combine multiple mixins for richer features.


HOTEL BOOKING:
    Base Booking extended into HotelBooking.
    Showed inheritance for hotel reservation systems.
    Used RewardMixin for loyalty points.
    Added CancelMixin for booking cancellation.
    Demonstrated flexibility in travel/hospitality apps.
    Separated core booking logic from extra services.
    Made the system modular and scalable.

   
MUSIC STREAMING:
    Base Song extended into Playlist.
    Showed inheritance for grouping songs.
    Used ShareMixin for sharing music.
    Added LikeMixin for user interactions.
    Modeled a music streaming platform.
    Demonstrated how mixins handle social features.
    Highlighted real-world OOP use in entertainment apps.


SMART VECHICLE:
    Base Vehicle extended into ElectricCar.
    Showed inheritance for modern vehicle specialization.
    Used GPSMixin for location tracking.
    Added LoggerMixin for activity logging.
    Applied OOP to IoT/Smart Car systems.
    Combined core functionality with modular features.
    Demonstrated real-world connected vehicle design.